{
 "approved": "2026-10-07 (demo-v3-sfx.mp4)",
 "rules": [
  "All files are HeyGen library clips (tools/heygen/library), trimmed and loudness-normalised (loudnorm I=-20). Use them as-is.",
  "Event time = the moment named in events.<role>.event. data-start = event_time - hit. If that is negative, use 0 (the hit lands slightly late, fine at video start).",
  "data-duration = sounds.<id>.duration, trimmed so the cue ends by the composition end.",
  "data-volume = events.<role>.volume (typing: 0.10-0.12).",
  "Volumes are relative to the raw voice. With the Auphonic voice (voice_studio.wav, -14 LUFS) multiply every SFX volume by 1.8 (creator, 2026-10-07: 1.0 'very low', 1.5 'a little bit louder, not too much', 1.8 chosen).",
  "Tracks: data-track-index 0-1 video layers, 2 voice, 3+ one per SFX cue. ids sfx-NN-<id>.",
  "Only sound events that are on screen. No sound for captions.",
  "Need a sound not in the kit: search HeyGen (scripts/heygen/sfx.py \"query\" -d), normalise to I=-20, propose it to the creator before adding it here."
 ],
